    "30698451-389d-43ce-b548-827c55ad66c4": {
      "type": "faq-diy",
      "blocks": {
        "13bb9ff7-7626-43dc-b72a-1af1ed19b7aa": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Why choose IPL technology for hair removal?",
            "cont": "<p>IPL, or intense pulsed light, uses strong pulses of broad-spectrum light to target hair at the root. The light is absorbed by the melanin in the hair follicle, where it is then converted into heat, resulting in thinner regrowth and eventually stopping hair growth altogether. Ulike IPL devices are CE-approved and offer a cost-effective, convenient solution compared to traditional methods of hair removal.</p>"
          }
        },
        "2ff93e1a-b179-42c4-ab58-fd8529be2357": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Does IPL work on all skin tones and hair colours?",
            "cont": "<p>IPL (Intense Pulsed Light) hair removal works by emitting intense light pulses that are absorbed by the pigment in the hair follicles. The absorbed light is then converted into heat, which targets the hair follicles and inhibits future hair growth.<br/><br/>It is important to note that IPL is most effective on individuals with lighter skin tones and darker hair colours. This is because the light energy is primarily absorbed by the melanin pigment in the hair. In individual's skin that's rich in melanin, the excess melanin can also absorb the light energy, leading to potential skin damage.<br/><br/>Similarly, IPL may not be as effective on individuals with light hair colours such as blonde, gray, or red. This is because these hair colours have less melanin content, making it challenging for the IPL device to target the hair follicles effectively.<br/><br/>To ensure the effectiveness and safety of IPL hair removal, we recommend users to refer to the provided skin tone chart before making a purchase.</p>",
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/pc_ccfeff71-e47f-48ed-b08b-aac83bb49d16.png",
            "image1": "shopify://shop_images/m_d00fd563-1ff5-41ee-acf6-26d42c1aaee6.png"
          }
        },
        "90eb32a1-93a6-4ea6-8811-9d8a427e58c6": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Is IPL right for me?",
            "cont": "<p>IPL hair removal device is not recommended if you have any of the following:</p><p>- A known skin disorder</p><p>- Skin diseases such as allergic dermatitis, eczema, etc.</p><p>- Photosensitive epilepsy or Photosensitivity</p><p>- Are menstruating, pregnant, or lactating</p><p>- Dark black or Sunburnt skin (please refer to the skin tone chart)</p><p>- Broken skin, a scab or healed wound, cancer or hemangioma</p><p>- Any artificial aesthetic, prosthetic, or plastic area</p><p>- Tattoo area</p>"
          }
        },
        "2a2d7031-162c-4034-80ec-feafe24584a3": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Is IPL safe?",
            "cont": "<p>Yes! IPL is a popular, well-researched option for safe and effective long-term hair removal. Ulike is FDA-cleared, UKCA, FCC, CE, and RoHS certified for safe at-home use. Also, all UV rays are filtered to protect your skin.</p>"
          }
        },
        "0f04a484-313b-44f3-8db5-87334c623ae3": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Are results permanent?",
            "cont": "<p>After completing the full treatment schedule, the treated area should be completely hairless or nearly so. However, when using your device, you are targeting hair follicles that are currently in the 'anagen' hair growth phase. It is possible that hairs not in the 'anagen' phase during treatment may still grow. You can simply use your Ulike device once every few weeks for touch-ups on these areas!</p>"
          }
        },
        "d79bd955-7402-4f6e-ab64-a52a5e6c37b7": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Can I use the device on all parts of my body?",
            "cont": "<p>Yes, you can use Ulike IPL devices on ALMOST every part of your body.<br/>However, please avoid using it on the following areas:<br/>-the eyes, or around the eyes<br/>-tattooed areas<br/>-parts of the skin with open wounds<br/>-birthmarks, moles or warts<br/>-areas that have plastic surgery<br/>Please refer to the above question \"Is IPL right for me\" for further information.</p>"
          }
        },
        "efdae77c-a49e-4c1c-91bc-ea1fc5bb0ae7": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Can I use it on my pubic area?",
            "cont": "<p>Yes, Ulike IPL devices can be used on the skin around your genitals, such as the bikini area, Brazilian wax area, and buttocks, but please do not use them directly on your genitals.</p>"
          }
        },
        "ec62c1a7-7ce9-428c-afd7-6e22907214ef": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Does IPL treatment hurt?",
            "cont": "<p>No, unlike laser hair removal, IPL hair removal is generally considered to be much safer and less painful. Additionally, Ulike is the only company that employs Sapphire Ice-Cooling patented technology to ensure completely painless sessions.</p>"
          }
        },
        "176cb9b5-d3ff-4aef-a580-e815624bd1aa": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "How often should I do treatments?",
            "cont": "<p>We recommend using the device three times a week for the first month to achieve the best results. After that, you can use it once every two weeks or once a month for touch-ups as needed.<br/><br/>Furthermore, we advise tailoring your usage according to your hair growth. If you encounter areas with thicker hair or stubbornness, feel free to elevate the power level and frequency of usage. Always be mindful of your skin's reaction and make adjustments to prevent any discomfort.</p>"
          }
        },
        "17a5f646-2280-4892-9d9d-7bd697ffe398": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Can men also use Ulike IPL devices?",
            "cont": "<p>Of course! Men and women can both use our devices</p>"
          }
        },
        "b7132d22-8b17-4d6f-88ee-725bccd6f493": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Do Ulike devices come with a warranty?",
            "cont": "<p>Yes! Every Ulike product comes with a 2 year limited manufacturer’s warranty. If your product stops working because of a manufacturing defect, it is eligible for a free replacement. Read more details about our warranties in our terms of service.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
